 really really  well and the video for that you can find  if you  look at the video description for this  one  i also got my classes totally lined up  for the coming semester meaning lined up  in the sense of i know what i'm teaching  not in the sense that the class shells  have been entirely built out that's  going to happen  partly this month and partly next month  for milwaukee institute of art and  design i am teaching existentialist  philosophy and literature and world  religions and for carthage college i am  teaching medieval philosophy so those  are going to be a lot of fun and those  will involve down the line shooting some  additional videos i mentioned the  stoicism today volume 3 book  that has been an awful lot of work not  just editing but doing all the things  that are required to get it into amazon  self-publishing fortunately my co-editor  shouldered the heaviest of the burdens  on that but even you know with that  there's a lot going on as well as  editing the stoicism today  blog along with my um my assistant  editor harold covley  so that's you know kept me going quite a  bit there's been some stuff that you  know had to be sorted out after stoicon  and after stoic week there's always some  follow-up stuff so that's been a lot  video production  i was hoping to get six half hour hegel  videos done this last month i actually  got only half of that but we did get  into a new  section the very final  part of the religion portion of the work  so that's pretty cool  i got two book review videos done  one that i gave a qualified endorsement  to one that i gave a full endorsement to  links to those can be found below as  well and  my my wife andy and i went on to  a podcast and also did a video about  stoicism and marriage with massimo  pigliucci and robert coulter had a great  conversation about that  wisdom for life you know we had the  radio show i also released a video  um and there was also an evil saddler  video that you might have noticed  popping up people seem to be into that  so i can't promise when and where he'll  show up again but i'm sure that we'll  see  more of that bastard um  and then what else i shot some i shot a  lot of uh footage for my  leguin earth c class um fantasy and  philosophy ursula k le guin's earthsea  it released a lot of videos on the  farthest shore and some on to hanu their  fourth novel  we are now finishing up the class so you  can guess my students have a lot of  videos that you haven't seen yet but  i'll be releasing them over time first  early releasing them to my patreon  supporters and then to the  general public  podcast work the saddlers lectures  podcast i finished releasing the podcast  episodes on miguel de una muno's tragic  sense of life then went into the ever  popular judith jarvis thompson the  trolley problem right  and then after that i i edited and  released some on freud's introductory  lecture 31 which is probably one of the  best places to start if you want to  understand freud's notion of the  personality and the unconscious and then  finally i've been releasing and editing  um podcast episodes on aristotle nick  mccann ethics books eight and nine not  super happy with the sound quality but  those were recorded before i started  using my  sound recorder with a lapel mic so the  sound is as good as it gets  after tweaking it and stuff like that i  also went on the radio a number of times  you know we have the wisdom for life  radio show that my  friend and co-host dan hayes and i  produce but i've been also going on to  riverwest radio as a  co-host for a different kind of show  their drive time with river west show  which is you know more topical  current events  riffing off of each other's stuff and  then interviewing some some guests and  so that's that's been a lot of fun  as well so that's  november  for the month of december the calendar  is particularly packed in the first two  weeks because i'm taking  for the most part the last two weeks as  just